{
  "what": "Single-pass extraction (classify, then read every field) by two models, same prompts, same pages, scored by archivist.eval.run_eval. 95% intervals are page-bootstrap.",
  "caveats": [
    "muse-spark-open is the run with the closing-bracket repair (baseten_api.close_brackets). Muse Spark Open, asked for JSON through the prompt, ended 75% of its ledger-card answers one } short (finish_reason stop); muse-spark-open-unrepaired is the first run, without the repair, where those pages failed to parse and are scored as omitted. The repair touches the form of an answer, never a value; 'closing_repairs' counts the answers it was applied to.",
    "reasoning_effort is low for both. Muse Spark Open always reasons and has no structured outputs: its schema is given in the prompt, Muse Spark 1.3's through response_format.",
    "The runs differ in the citation step (run.json 'citations'); field accuracy and error rate do not depend on the boxes.",
    "dev is development data (D26); val is development data too. Nothing here was scored on the frozen test set."
  ],
